t_transfer_those_aftermarket_products_to_pixel_nord_or_blackview","use_the_iphone_6_6s_and_7_posts_as_individual_dated_anecdotes_not_rates_causal_proof_or_candidate_model_evidence","separate_physical_operation_component_wear_repair_access_manufacturer_support_security_app_compatibility_and_daily_task_satisfaction","use_screen_burn_in_service_life_repairability_and_modularity_as_general_frameworks_not_exact_model_outcomes","do_not_use_the_planned_obsolescence_background_to_accuse_any_vendor_of_intent","treat_security_support_as_a_field_to_verify_from_current_primary_sources_not_as_a_fact_established_by_this_packet","name_no_universal_2031_winner_and_make_no_longevity_guarantee"],"scenario":"I want to buy one phone now and still use it happily and safely in 2031. The research packet contains old or renewed seller snapshots for a Google Pixel 4a with 5G, a OnePlus Nord N10, and a Blackview BL5000; an aftermarket DEJI battery kit listed only for specific iPhone X models; and a Dahkoiz case listed only for the Galaxy A13 5G. It also contains three dated personal reports: an iPhone 6s kept since 2016 with several aging symptoms, a five-year iPhone 7 with an unresolved microphone problem after battery service, and an eight-year iPhone 6 that still functioned while several apps stopped supporting iOS 12.5. General background covers screen burn-in, service life, repairability, modular smartphones, and planned obsolescence. The packet has no verified current-unit condition report, no current support-end promise for a 2026 candidate, no controlled phone-to-phone longevity study, and no population failure rates.","target":"Produce a source-bounded buying analysis for a phone intended to remain pleasant and safe through 2031. First audit the three frozen phone listings, including the Nord page's conflicting review counts, and keep all seller statements at listing scope. Then use the three iPhone posts only to show how different physical, performance, repair, and app-support endpoints can appear in individual long-use stories. Explain why physical operation, manufacturer service or security support, essential-app compatibility, and repairability are separate. Convert the general mechanism pages into a practical current-evidence checklist, not a vendor accusation or model score. End with a table that a buyer can fill for genuinely current exact models and regions: condition and channel, written operating-system and security support end dates from current primary sources, essential apps, carrier compatibility, battery, screen, and port service, parts and manuals, repair prices and data effects, warranty, return window, accessory fit, daily-task trial results, maintenance and backup steps, and explicit exit triggers. If those cells are not filled, defer rather than naming a winner. Even a passing candidate remains a conditional choice, not a promise that it will survive or feel good in 2031."},"graph_motif":"causal_or_evolution_explanation","graph_node_to_step_id":{"bridge_current_2031_matrix":"B6","bridge_repairability_audit":"B1","decision_conditional_2031_selection":"D1","ev_a13_case_snapshot":"E1","ev_blackview_listing_snapshot":"E2","ev_iphone_x_battery_kit_snapshot":"E3","ev_nord_n10_listing_snapshot":"E4","ev_pixel_4a_listing_snapshot":"E5","mechanism_exact_aftermarket_boundary":"B2","mechanism_long_use_anecdote_boundary":"B3","mechanism_physical_policy_layers":"B4","mechanism_seller_snapshot_boundary":"B5","prop_iphone_6_app_scope":"E6","prop_iphone_6s_long_use_scope":"E7","prop_iphone_7_five_year_scope":"E8","prop_modular_smartphone_scope":"E9","prop_planned_obsolescence_scope":"E10","prop_repairability_framework_scope":"E11","prop_screen_burn_in_scope":"E12","prop_service_life_scope":"E13"},"motif_compilation_schema":"graph_motif_compilation_v1","topology_checks":{"has_decision":true,"has_mechanism":true,"has_state_or_proposition":true,"mechanism_is_derived":true}},"directly_scorable_gold":false,"discovery_parameters":{"max_expansion